WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.920
We must all turn our backs 
upon the horrors of the past.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.840
We must look to the future.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.880
We must build a kind 
of United States of Europe.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.600
The European Community means 
peace between France and Germany,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.520
and reduction of  national egoisms.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.520
Being awarded the Nobel Peace Prize 
is actually being given a mission,

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.160
one to promote peace, the notion 
of peace, wherever possible.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.480
Europe was not created. 
That is why we had the war.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.440
Europe won't be created in one go.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.360
It will be created by means of 
concrete achievements.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.360
Personally, I would be very upset 
if Europe were damaged

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.720
during these critical times.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.720
We have problems but we nevertheless 
stick together as it has a great value.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.680
That's what this prize means to me.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:14.920
Why did we really want 
to create Europe

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.840
right after 
the Second World War?

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.960
Countries fought each other 
during WWI and WWII,

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.400
there were brutal military conflicts, 
but that is impossible today.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.960
I couldn't pick a gun up now and fight 
a friend from Germany or France.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.280
It's not possible.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.960
This first common market,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.880
these first supranational institutions

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.920
mean Europe is starting to unite.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.640
This Nobel Peace Prize 
acts as a uniting factor

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:03.200
at a time when the economy 
could actually mean "economic war".

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.840
Come on, look back for a moment! 

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.040
Ask yourselves how Europe looked like 
fifty years ago.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.360
Solidarity is being rather 
sorely tested at the moment

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.240
but it's true that it may be 
a good idea to remember that,

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.560
unlike our parents and grandparents, 
we haven't experienced war.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.480
Only with a strong, united Europe

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:38.240
can the Europeans, and the world, 
really prosper.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:47.640
Since the Wall came down I've felt 
I'm finally living at the right time,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.160
because the building of the Wall was 
a negative turning point in my life.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.520
Warmly welcome to our family.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.280
Our new Europe is born.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.280
Europe hasn't been created just for us 
but for all European countries.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.040
Opening our arms to these countries is 
wonderful, it's letting our heart speak.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.040
We can live normally, 
we don't have to be afraid of anything.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.000
We may get to know 
the rest of the world.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.840
1st May 2004, 

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.400
I was among all those 
who were moved to tears

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.680
because it was such a symbolic moment.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:39.400
Our return to the community of nations,

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.800
where Poland had to find its place.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.440
I am very proud of this and 
I would like all young people,

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.000
in fact not only the young 
but everyone in Poland,

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.800
to feel as proud as I am.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.000
I am thirty years old and, 
as a child, I survived this war.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.520
I have never visited Europe

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:22.080
and I would like to visit Europe 
and be a European citizen.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.080
I would like to see  
how people live there.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.760
That would be a great feeling.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.600
We have today been able to

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.560
give a very clear message  
to the Western Balkans:

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:39.000
they will become part of our family.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.960
I was very small 
when I lost my mother during the war.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.760
Some things you can never forget 
but we have to look ahead,

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:59.440
because of our children, 
because of Bosnia and Herzegovina,

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.440
because of the future  
of Bosnia and Herzegovina.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.520
We will never be reminded enough

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.640
of how much this peace, 
now so deeply rooted,

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.320
is a revolution

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.440
compared to a history of never-ending,

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.640
dramatic and bloody conflicts. 

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.600
All I can say is...

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.040
carry on fighting with peaceful means

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.120
so that Europe remains united.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.680
I love Europe.

